n2p2 is an open-source software package that implements
high-dimensional neural network potentials based on the
Behler-Parrinello method for computational physics and chemistry.

It allows to use existing neural network potential parameterizations to
predict energies and forces in conjunction with the MD software
LAMMPS.

n2p2 is an optional dependency of lammps.

Dependency openmpi4 is strictly required for Slackware 32-bit. Users of
64-bit systems can better use openmpi as dependency.

Citation
Andreas Singraber, mpbircher, Sam Reeve, David W.H. Swenson,
Jérémy Lauret, & philippedavid. (2021). 
CompPhysVienna/n2p2: Version 2.1.4 (Version v2.1.4) [Computer software]
Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4750573
